[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]
If you have many add-ons that define a lot of keybindings, you might hit keybindings shadow limit imposed by the ESO client. If your keybinds stop saving, you have hit the shadow limit.

I plan to break up the keybinds into separate modules that you'll be able to disable if you don't use any of their keybinds.

Additionally, I'm aware of the following issues that I, unfortunately, cannot do anything about currently:

[LIST]
[*]Focus primary search box doesn't work in Guild Store > Browse with AwesomeGuildStore, as I cannot reliably look up the control.
[*][I]Show next subtab[/I] and [I]Show previous subtab[/I] don't work in the Alchemy window, as the tabs don't have proper descriptors.
[*][I]Show next subtab[/I] and [I]Show previous subtab[/I] don't work in the Guild Store with AwesomeGuildStore, as AwesomeGuildStore doesn't use a proper ZO_MenuBar.
[*][I]Show next subtab[/I] and [I]Show previous subtab[/I] don't work in the Outfit Station window, as the tabs don't have proper descriptors.
[*]The [I]Dungeon Finder[/I] and [I]Battlegrounds[/I] keybinds select the wrong entry in the navigation list of the group window. This appears to be a bug in the ESO UI.
[/LIST]
